 ### [Sparse Coding (K-SVD)](1018-sparse-coding-k-svd.md)
-Sparse Coding (K-SVD) compresses volume rendering data by learning an overcomplete dictionary from rendered images and representing image blocks as sparse linear combinations of dictionary atoms. It sets itself apart from prescribed basis methods like [Wavelet and Pyramid Transforms](3856-wavelet-and-pyramid-transforms.md) by adapting the basis to the specific statistical structure of the volume data, and from [Vector Quantization for Volumetric Radiance Fields](1870-vector-quantization-for-volumetric-radiance-fields.md) by allowing multiple atoms per block, which reduces reconstruction error at the cost of higher encoding complexity.
